and this is no different,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
this crazy thing that happened
there where they were

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
going to try to deny the peopl
of Detroit the right

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:19.145 line:92%
to have their vote counted

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:22.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We've obviously talked
about Joe Biden

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fact
that you liked him.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.020 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You met him at a DNC.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your first interactio
with him like?

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I met him at
the Democratic Convention

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Boston in 2004, and I was
in the presidential box,

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is not
where I'm usually found.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:42.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
But President Jimmy Carter had
invited me to sit with him

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.536 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the convention.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
And of course this drove
Fox News

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.208 line:92%
and the right wing crazy.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.443 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But in one of those --

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know where they have
those luxury boxes

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the basketball

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the football game
or whatever,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.984 size:78% position:39%
I didn't realize this
but you actually --

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a whole area behin
the box

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.055 line:92%
that's full of catered food.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
So naturally I left my sea
and went back

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.126 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to get something to eat,

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in through the door
comes Joe Biden.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.028 line:92%
I'd never met him before.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
He sees me and he just goes,
like, "Holy --"

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.402 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Expletive.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he comes at me,
he's all smiles

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's shakin' my --
grabbin' my hand.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.343 size:78% position:39%
"Oh, God, I've always
wanted to meet you.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.244 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it --

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wow, mother [bleep],
this is something. Wow!"

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's just dropping F-bombs
And I'm like, "Whoa."

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:35.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we start talking,
he wants to talk about

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.723 line:92%
my dad working in the factor

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my mom was a clerk
and this and that.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, I knew
he always said

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was from the working class,
but I never saw it

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he always had thos
nicely tailored suits,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
perfect teeth.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
And within ten or 15 minutes
I realized,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.106 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"Wow, he is one of us.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
He did come from
where I came from."

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:58.411
There's no cameras around,
it not a show or anything.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.612 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He's just being himself.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think what Bernie
had said about him,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he was a good
and decent person.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I guess in those minutes
there with him, you know,

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.456 line:92%
I don't know, 15 minutes -

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you make up your mind
about somebody in 15 minutes

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess I decided that
he was that person.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:19.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have felt through
the campaign,

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though
I was helping Bernie,

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:26.139 size:88% position:44%
I think that I felt that
if he became president,

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were going to
have a chance.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even though maybe
our politics

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.212 size:88% position:44% line:92%
didn't line up entirely,

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.447 size:84% position:42%
we were going to have
a better chance getting

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
our thing through.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like -- like --
-There's really a lot

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
of parallels with what
you're saying

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:41.487
to what Bernie has said
about Joe over the years,

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is one, he always make
clear we're different

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a lot of things
politically.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two, though, he always
makes clear that

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.363 line:92%
he really likes Joe Biden.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.700
And he thinks that he can get on
the phone with him if need be.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:58.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously one of the thing
progressives are up against no

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the fact that
the president-elect

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.341 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is a bit more moderate.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you -- how do you feel lik
progressives have to try

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
to influence policy
moving forward?

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We may have to make sure
our voices are heard,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have to be heard
right now

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:15.154
while he's picking the cabinet
while they're deciding policy.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.390 line:92%
This is a very critical phase.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so -- but I believe that
Joe Biden will listen.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.162 line:92%
We may not always get our way,

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
we may not get him
to agree with us on everything

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.066 size:84% position:42%
but I think that it's
kind of like if he says

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.168 line:92%
he's against Medicare for All.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if --
when we get the Senate,

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if we pass
a Medicare for All bill

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.475
and it goes to his desk,
he's not going to veto it.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.111 size:84% position:42%
He's not going to say,
"No, I'm -- what, what?

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody gets health care
No way!"

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:41.914 line:92%
He's not going to do that.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
If he's for $12 an hour
minimum wage

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the bill says $15
because we --

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
the progressive part of this
which is really

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
the majority because
the majority of Americans

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
want a $15 an hour
minimum wage.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
They want women paid
the same as men.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
They believe that
climate change is real.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:05:00.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a progressive country.
I've said this many times.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if the progressive
legislation comes on his desk,

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to believe
he's going to sign this.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's not going to -- he no
going to send it back.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a better chance
with him.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously better than if Trump
had won another term.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:17.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm actually --
I'm surprised, frankly.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.520
I have to say, I don't kno
how you feel about this.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
If COVID hadn't come along
would --

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:26.559 size:78% position:39% line:92%
would Trump have won?

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would he have got
that second term?

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.463 line:92%
Because here's the thing.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've wondered about this
for months.

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:36.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, an authoritarian
totalitarian leader

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:41.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
would relish to have the
opportunity to tell the people

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:46.045 size:84% position:42%
"You will wear a mask,
you will stay indoors."

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:48.715
You know, that's what an
authoritarian wants to do.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:50.450 line:92%
They want to give orders,

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also wants to be seen
as the hero.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:57.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Take the reins of this virus
kill the virus, succeed.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not Trump.
No, the opposite.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:02.095 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He doesn't do anything.

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:04.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just ignores it
or tries to pretend

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:05.965 line:92%
it will go away by Easter.

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:09.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now we have
a quarter million dead.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.604 line:92%
Seth, a quarter million dead

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the same exact number
of people as if --

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:17.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you wake up tomorrow mornin
and you look at your phone

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.212 line:92%
and it says, "Breaking news,

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:22.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Richmond, Virginia,
has been annihilated.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Everyone is dead."

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:27.453 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That would be such --

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
what would that do
to our collective heads?

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:34.327
And yet here we are tonigh
at a quarter million dead.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're not acting like
Richmond, Virginia,

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.197 line:92%
has just been annihilated.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're not acting like
there are now --

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:44.303 line:92%
there's now a 9/11 every two -

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:47.774 line:92%
every two or three days now.

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're -- I don't know
what it is,

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:54.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we need Biden and his team
to take these reins,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.283 size:88% position:44%
to get this country --
as Fauci said this week,

00:06:57.283 --> 00:07:01.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
we need a national mandate
of how to deal with this virus

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:03.723 line:92%
not a state by state by state.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to get back,
talk about that.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back with mor
from Michael Moore.

